# 0010. Alt-h/j/k/l moves across nvim splits and tmux panes (smart-splits)

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-07

## Context
nvim runs inside tmux; moving between nvim splits and tmux panes needed different keys.

## Decision
smart-splits.nvim binds Alt-h/j/k/l (move) and Alt-Shift-h/j/k/l (resize). It loads at start so
it can mark the pane as nvim; the tmux side (`~/projects/tmux/conf/keys.conf`) forwards the keys
when `@pane-is-vim` is set. At the screen edge movement stops (`at_edge = "stop"`), as in tmux.

## Alternatives
Not recorded at the time. `<C-h>`/`<C-l>` were not used: they are side-scroll keys here.

## Rationale
One set of keys for one mental model: panes and splits are the same thing.

## Consequences
- The binding is split across two repos (nvim and tmux) that must agree.
- Upstream option renames are silent: `at_edge` was ignored for weeks until fixed in PR #2.

## References
- `lua/plugins/tmux.lua`, PR #1, PR #2
